Roles & Responsibilities

Descriptions:
-Must have at least 6 years experiences in network design and implementation, network hardware configuration, network troubleshooting and network performance tuning network and system administration;

 -Must have at least 6years experiences in managing network products such as Cisco, F5, and etc;

- Must have at least 6 years experiences in administering Windows Server and Linux Operating Systems



Responsibilities:
- Must have sound knowledge of various network protocols and topologies, including LAN, WAN, switches, routers and servers;

- Should preferably have experience in managing Network Access Control (NAC) System such as ClearPass, SolarWinds, and Infoblox.

The Programmer shall be required to:

a. Administer and troubleshoot network system infrastructure;

b. Administer and troubleshoot Windows Server and Linux Operating Systems;

c. Perform installation and upgrading of network system and servers;

d. Perform installation of operating systems, software applications and device drivers on the Servers;

e. Perform backup and recovery of network devices and servers;

f. Perform simple scripting in Windows Server and Linux environment;

g. Perform any other tasks related to network and server hardware and software, end-user support and project works as may be assigned by the supervisor;

h. Able to administer Clear Pass Network Access Control, SolarWinds, and Infoblox.
